Chamfers: a walked chamfer's guide keeps to its edges where it takes the
tangents of the analytic blends before and after it (mitcad#263).

The case: a chain of edges joined at slight angles (1.4 degrees), arcs
between curved stretches, its arcs chamfered as cones (ChFiKPart) and its
stretches walked. ChFi3d_PerformElSpine makes the guide of a stretch start
and end with the tangents of the cones' end sections (GeomLib's
AdjustExtremity), which deformed the whole curve: on a stretch of 16.6 mm
the guide ran up to 0.11 mm off its edge, and a chamfer's contacts, at its
distances from the guide, moved with it (a chamfer of 0.263 became one of
0.18 in the middle of the stretch).

- For a chamfer (whose guide may be deformed by a hundredth of its distance
  at most, 0381), the guide takes those tangents within its smallest
  distance of each end only (ChFi3d_AdjustGuideEndsLocally): knots are
  inserted there and the two poles at the end moved, the tangent's length
  kept. Elsewhere it is the edge's curve as before the adjustment. Other
  blends, and ends extended past the spine, are unchanged.

